From 606ed6931fe0b362bd13f8508abdc6c582966983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filip Spanne <filip.spanne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 13:19:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] elanpress: Add driver for ELAN press-type sensors
 (04f3:0c6e)

The ELAN 0c6e (found in ASUS ROG Flow X13 and other ASUS laptops) is a
press-type sensor that streams raw 150x52 frames using the same bulk
protocol as the swipe sensors handled by the elan driver. It was listed
in the elan driver's id table, but treating it as a swipe sensor stitches
near-identical frames of a resting finger into unusable images, so
enrollment stored garbage templates and verification always failed.

The imaged area (about 7.5x2.6 mm) is also too small for NBIS minutiae
matching: cross-press genuine bozorth3 scores stay below impostor scores,
which was validated by replaying USB captures of the Windows driver
through the virtual-image device.

Instead, this driver does match-on-host with image correlation, like the
Windows driver: enrollment stores several processed touch images in the
print, and matching computes zero-mean normalized cross-correlation over
translations. On capture data of the same finger, genuine presses of
overlapping regions correlate at 0.59-0.93 while impostor probes stay
below 0.48; the acceptance threshold is 0.55.

Verified on hardware (ASUS ROG Flow X13 GV301RC): enrollment and
verification work through fprintd.

Original commit 34fc394 on github.com/filip-rs/libfprint (branch
elanpress, on top of v1.94.10). Rebased onto v1.94.100: the driver list
in meson.build changed to a dictionary, so the entry is now
'elanpress': { 'endian_dependent': true }.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
